Sales Performance Dashboard | Power BI

Project Overview

This project focuses on analyzing business performance using Microsoft Power BI. The dashboard provides insights into revenue, costs, profitability, customer trends, brand performance, product preferences, and customer income levels.

Tools & Skills

* Microsoft Power BI
* Power Query
* Data Cleaning and Transformation
* KPI Creation
* Data Visualization
* Business Intelligence and Insight Generation

Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)

* Total Revenue: $3.11M
* Total Cost: $2.17M
* Total Profit: $931.905K
* Total Customers: 250

Key Business Insights

1. Revenue Performance

The business generated approximately $3.11 million in revenue, with the yearly revenue chart indicating strong overall performance in 2023.

2. Profitability

Total profit reached approximately $931.9K against total costs of $2.17M, indicating that the business generated a positive profit after covering its costs.

3. Top-Performing Brands

Apple recorded the highest profit at approximately $197K. Lenovo and Samsung followed at around $160K each, while Dell recorded the lowest profit among the displayed brands at approximately $126K.

4. Product Purchases by Color

White products recorded the highest purchase quantity at approximately 6K, followed by gray products at 5.2K. Black products recorded the lowest quantity at around 4.1K.

This suggests that white products were the most purchased color in the dataset.

5. Profit by Customer Income Level

Medium-income customers generated the highest profit at approximately $17K, compared with $12.5K from low-income customers and $12K from high-income customers.

6. Monthly Customer Trends

The dashboard shows a decline in monthly customer counts from approximately 90 to 77 across the displayed periods. This trend may require further investigation to understand changes in customer activity.

Recommendations

* Investigate monthly customer declines and identify opportunities to improve customer retention.
* Analyze the factors contributing to Apple’s stronger profitability.
* Review product demand by color to support inventory planning.
* Explore the purchasing behavior of medium-income customers to identify opportunities for growth.

Conclusion

This project demonstrates my ability to clean and transform data, create KPIs, build interactive Power BI visualizations, and translate business data into actionable insights.
